{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":20,"code":"PRO","name":"Proverbs","testament":"OT"},"chapter":25,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PRO 25:1"},"These ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," also proverbs of Solomon, which the men of Hezekiah king of Judah copied out. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PRO 25:2"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["It is"]}," the glory of God to conceal a thing: but the honour of kings ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," to search out a matter. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PRO 25:3"},"The heaven for height, and the earth for depth, and the heart of kings ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," unsearchable. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"PRO 25:4"},"Take away the dross from the silver, and there shall come forth a vessel for the finer. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"PRO 25:5"},"Take away the wicked ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["from"]}," before the king, and his throne shall be established in righteousness. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"PRO 25:6"},"Put not forth thyself in the presence of the king, and stand not in the place of great ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["men: "]},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"PRO 25:7"},"For better ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it is"]}," that it be said unto thee, Come up hither; than that thou shouldest be put lower in the presence of the prince whom thine eyes have seen. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"PRO 25:8"},"Go not forth hastily to strive, lest ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["thou know not"]}," what to do in the end thereof, when thy neighbour hath put thee to shame. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"PRO 25:9"},"Debate thy cause with thy neighbour ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["himself;"]}," and discover not a secret to another: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"PRO 25:10"},"Lest he that heareth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it"]}," put thee to shame, and thine infamy turn not away. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"PRO 25:11"},"A word fitly spoken ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is like"]}," apples of gold in pictures of silver. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"PRO 25:12"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["As"]}," an earring of gold, and an ornament of fine gold, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["so is"]}," a wise reprover upon an obedient ear. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"PRO 25:13"},"As the cold of snow in the time of harvest, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["so is"]}," a faithful messenger to them that send him: for he refresheth the soul of his masters. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"PRO 25:14"},"Whoso boasteth himself of a false gift ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is like"]}," clouds and wind without rain. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"PRO 25:15"},"By long forbearing is a prince persuaded, and a soft tongue breaketh the bone. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"PRO 25:16"},"Hast thou found honey? eat so much as is sufficient for thee, lest thou be filled therewith, and vomit it. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"PRO 25:17"},"Withdraw thy foot from thy neighbour’s house; lest he be weary of thee, and ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["so"]}," hate thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"PRO 25:18"},"A man that beareth false witness against his neighbour ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is "]},"a maul, and a sword, and a sharp arrow. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"PRO 25:19"},"Confidence in an unfaithful man in time of trouble ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is like "]},"a broken tooth, and a foot out of joint. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"PRO 25:20"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["As"]}," he that taketh away a garment in cold weather, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and as "]},"vinegar upon nitre, so ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," he that singeth songs to an heavy heart. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"PRO 25:21"},"If thine enemy be hungry, give him bread to eat; and if he be thirsty, give him water to drink: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"PRO 25:22"},"For thou shalt heap coals of fire upon his head, and the LORD shall reward thee. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:22"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"23","sid":"PRO 25:23"},"The north wind driveth away rain: so ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["doth"]}," an angry countenance a backbiting tongue. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:23"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"24","sid":"PRO 25:24"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["It is"]}," better to dwell in the corner of the housetop, than with a brawling woman and in a wide house. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:24"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"25","sid":"PRO 25:25"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["As"]}," cold waters to a thirsty soul, so ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," good news from a far country. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:25"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"26","sid":"PRO 25:26"},"A righteous man falling down before the wicked ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is as"]}," a troubled fountain, and a corrupt spring. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:26"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"27","sid":"PRO 25:27"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["It is "]},"not good to eat much honey: so ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["for men "]},"to search their own glory ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is not "]},"glory. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:27"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"28","sid":"PRO 25:28"},"He that ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["hath"]}," no rule over his own spirit ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is like "]},"a city ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that is"]}," broken down, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," without walls. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PRO 25:28"}]}]}
